CON-06: scale snow plowed to another subcatchment by both subcatchments' areas

SnowSolver::plowSnow() copied legacy snow_plowSnow(): the depth added to the
receiving subcatchment's pervious pack was sfrac[4] * exc * fArea_j / fArea_m,
a ratio of area fractions only, so the plowed volume was multiplied by
A_m / A_j. Include the ratio of the two non-LID areas. Same change as
CON-06_swmm530.patch.

Apply from the root of a Stormwater-Management-Model checkout at cb3e192b:
    git apply CON-06_swmm600.patch

diff --git a/src/engine/hydrology/Snow.cpp b/src/engine/hydrology/Snow.cpp
index 5f27b5c..4c27d8a 100644
--- a/src/engine/hydrology/Snow.cpp
+++ b/src/engine/hydrology/Snow.cpp
@@ -542,8 +542,24 @@ void SnowSolver::plowSnow(SimulationContext& ctx, double dt, const double* snowf
             int m = soa_.to_subcatch[uj];
             if (m < n) {
                 auto target_perv = static_cast<std::size_t>(m * N_SUBAREAS + SNOW_PERV);
-                if (soa_.fArea[target_perv] > 0.0) {
-                    double f = soa_.fArea[plow_idx] / soa_.fArea[target_perv];
+                // fArea are fractions of each subcatchment's own non-LID
+                // area, so the transfer must also scale by the ratio of
+                // those areas (legacy snow_getSnowCover's area basis).
+                // The ratio is 1 when the context holds no subcatchment
+                // areas (the solver driven on its own, as in unit tests).
+                auto um = static_cast<std::size_t>(m);
+                const auto& area = ctx.subcatches.area;
+                const auto& lid  = ctx.subcatches.total_lid_area_ft2;
+                double a_j = 1.0;
+                double a_m = 1.0;
+                if (uj < area.size() && um < area.size()) {
+                    const double ucf_a = ucf::UCF(ucf::LANDAREA, ctx.options);
+                    a_j = area[uj] / ucf_a - (uj < lid.size() ? lid[uj] : 0.0);
+                    a_m = area[um] / ucf_a - (um < lid.size() ? lid[um] : 0.0);
+                }
+                if (soa_.fArea[target_perv] > 0.0 && a_m > 0.0) {
+                    double f = soa_.fArea[plow_idx] * a_j /
+                               (soa_.fArea[target_perv] * a_m);
                     const double moved = soa_.sfrac[sf + 4] * exc * f;
